der: Possible in diabetics but insufficient evidence for this mechanism yet", "Exertional Syndrome: No context of recent physical stress aligning with EAH or EHS"], "alarm_features": ["Severe hypertension (BP 197/128 mmHg)", "Mild fever (37.5°C)", "Obesity with physical signs of chronic constipation", "Vascular exam findings (weak lower-extremity pulses)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "GI Obstruction and Mechanical Complications", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.417424029930849, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Signs of mechanical obstruction weaken B4’s plausibility, but no definitive exclusion criteria are met.", "Prior appendectomy scar increases adhesion-related GI obstruction (Option A) under B1."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of cramping and asymmetrical distension weakens B1 as the primary explanation.", "Absence of cramping or asymmetric distension contradicts a primary mechanical obstruction (B1), favoring non-mechanical GI dysfunction."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of prior abdominal surgeries (scar relevance)", "Timing of symptoms relative to meals", "Presence of crampy abdominal pain or distension"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Abdominal CT with enteric contrast", "Physical exam for high-pitched bowel sounds"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Neurogenic Gastrointestinal Dysfunction", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.04426173306420619, "posterior": 0.04711664535374662, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Absence of jaundice and typical biliary signs weakens B5, though high-fat meal association maintains neutrality.", "Physical findings of mechanical bowel and vascular etiology provide no direct evidence for B2 and minimal against."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of chronic constipation", "Diabetic neuropathy symptoms (e.g., peripheral numbness)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Abdominal wall sensory testing", "Gastric emptying study"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Infectious Enteritis", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.038901913825962454, "posterior": 0.04141111408044134, "danger": 0.4, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Low-grade fever and subacute timeline are inconsistent with norovirus, but risk exposure maintains a weak_for labeling."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Recent travel/exposure to infected individuals (wife's cruise)", "Presence of low-grade fever"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Stool PCR for norovirus", "Rapid antigen test"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Chronic Aortoiliac Occlusive Syndrome", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3227302771001847, "posterior": 0.34354660241134155, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Severe hypertension and weak pulses moderately support vascular obstruction (B4), though claudication absence limits confidence."], "evidence_against": ["Signs of mechanical obstruction weaken B4’s plausibility, but no definitive exclusion criteria are met.", "Lack of claudication or sexual dysfunction weakens B4 as a primary cause but does not rule it out."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Leg/claudication symptoms during ambulation", "History of sexual dysfunction"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Aortoiliac Doppler ultrasound", "Ankle-brachial index (ABI)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "urgency"}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Biliary/Gallbladder Disease", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.06450068923869491, "danger": 0.65, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of jaundice and fever strongly excludes biliary/gallbladder disease (B5) as the primary cause."]}, "B6": {"id": "B6", "label": "Inflammatory Bowel Disease", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.08600091898492654, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Prior appendectomy is a simpler explanation than IBD surgery, reducing B6’s likelihood."]}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Adhesion-related Bowel Obstruction", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.2087120149654245, "posterior": 0.2087120149654245, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of prior abdominal surgeries (RLQ scar suggests appendectomy)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Abdominal CT with enteric contrast (adhesions vs impacted stool)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Impa